All 16 functions from `KernSmooth/R/all.R` have been converted to Python and written to `/groups/jli9/Yufei/python-KernSmooth/ablation/conversion_guides/no_guides/10/all.R/`, one JSON file per function, with no conversion guides used anywhere in the pipeline (each sub-agent was explicitly instructed to skip guide-based steps and instead reimplement the underlying Fortran algorithms natively from source).

Conversion order followed dependency levels (leaves → roots):
1. `linbin`, `rlbin`
2. `blkest`, `cpblock`, `linbin2D`, `bkfe`, `locpoly`, `sdiag`, `sstdiag`, `bkde`
3. `bkde2D`, `dpih`, `dpik`, `dpill`, `.onAttach`, `.onUnload`

Several agents independently validated their output against the R reference or theoretical values (e.g., `blkest` matched real R output to 9 significant digits, `bkfe` matched the theoretical normal-density constant, `locpoly` converged to the true derivative as gridsize increased), and `dpill`'s agent correctly caught a subtle R lazy-evaluation quirk where the `range.x` default reflects trimmed rather than raw data.
